{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790439480856,"sessionID":"ses_f2180005effeUp6G3SA93ShUgR","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_cc942d5e049e4824b3e19051","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Explore codebase structure","prompt":"Explore the codebase at /workspace thoroughly. I need to understand:\n1. The directory structure (key folders and files)\n2. The contents of res://data/units/unit_stats.gd (where unit stats and Team enum are defined)\n3. The contents of res://scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.gd and battle_unit.tscn\n4. Any existing custom_nodes/ directory\n5. How BattleUnit is defined\n6. The UnitStats resource/singleton structure\n7. Any collision layer/mask conventions used\n\nReturn the full contents of all relevant files and the directory structure.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"<task id=\"ses_f217f98a8ffeEF0MkZuom37Ir3\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nHere is a thorough breakdown of the entire codebase at `/workspace`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Directory Structure\n\n```\n/workspace/\n├── .godot/                              # Godot editor cache (not committed to VCS)\n│   ├── .gdignore\n│   ├── global_script_class_cache.cfg    # Registered global class names (BattleUnit, UnitStats)\n│   ├── scene_groups_cache.cfg           # Groups: \"sentries\" and \"raiders\"\n│   ├── uid_cache.bin\n│   └── editor/\n│       ├── filesystem_cache10\n│       ├── main.tscn-folding-...cfg\n│       └── project_metadata.cfg\n├── data/\n│   ├── enemies/\n│   │   └── zombie.tres                  # UnitStats resource: team=ENEMY(1), attack_range=1\n│   └── units/\n│       ├── bjorn.tres                   # UnitStats resource: team=PLAYER(0), attack_range=3\n│       ├── unit_stats.gd                # UnitStats class definition + Team enum\n│       └── unit_stats.gd.uid            # UID: uid://6g3nmkgoab16\n├── scenes/\n│   ├── main.tscn                        # Test scene with 3 BattleUnit instances\n│   └── battle_unit/\n│       ├── battle_unit.gd               # BattleUnit class (extends Area2D)\n│       ├── battle_unit.gd.uid           # UID: uid://co1dno2t5o6ga\n│       └── battle_unit.tscn             # BattleUnit scene (Area2D + CollisionShape2D)\n├── project.godot                        # Project: \"Detect Range Target Finder\", Godot 4.4, gl_compatibility\n└── task_config.json                     # Task instructions for implementing detect_range/target_finder\n```\n\n**Notable:** There is **no `custom_nodes/` directory yet** -- `task_config.json` instructs creating it at `res://custom_nodes/`.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Full File Contents\n\n### `/workspace/data/units/unit_stats.gd` (UnitStats Resource + Team Enum)\n\n```gdscript\nclass_name UnitStats\nextends Resource\n\nenum Team {PLAYER, ENEMY}\n\nconst MAX_ATTACK_RANGE := 5\n\n@export var team: Team\n@export_range(1, MAX_ATTACK_RANGE) var attack_range: int = 1\n```\n\n**Key points:**\n- `UnitStats` is a `Resource` (not a singleton). Multiple `.tres` instances exist (bjorn, zombie).\n- `Team` enum: `{PLAYER=0, ENEMY=1}` -- Godot by default assigns integer values starting from 0.\n- `attack_range` is clamped to `[1, MAX_ATTACK_RANGE]` (`[1, 5]`).\n\n---\n\n### `/workspace/scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.gd` (BattleUnit Script)\n\n```gdscript\nclass_name BattleUnit\nextends Area2D\n\n@export var stats: UnitStats: set = _set_stats\n\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tif stats:\n\t\t_set_stats(stats)\n\n\nfunc _set_stats(value: UnitStats) -> void:\n\tstats = value\n\t\n\tif not stats or not is_node_ready():\n\t\treturn\n\t\n\tstats = value.duplicate()\n\tcollision_layer = stats.team + 1\n```\n\n**Key points:**\n- `BattleUnit` extends `Area2D`.\n- `stats` is an exported `UnitStats`. When set (via editor or `_ready`):\n  1. It **duplicates** the resource (so instances don't share the same `UnitStats` ref).\n  2. Sets `collision_layer` to `stats.team + 1`, which means:\n     - `Team.PLAYER` (0) -> collision layer **1**\n     - `Team.ENEMY` (1) -> collision layer **2**\n- There are no `onready` variables for `detect_range` or `target_finder` yet -- these are yet to be implemented per `task_config.json`.\n\n---\n\n### `/workspace/scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.tscn` (BattleUnit Scene)\n\n```ini\n[gd_scene load_steps=3 format=3]\n\n[ext_resource type=\"Script\" path=\"res://scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.gd\" id=\"1_battle_unit\"]\n[ext_resource type=\"Resource\" path=\"res://data/units/bjorn.tres\" id=\"2_stats\"]\n\n[sub_resource type=\"RectangleShape2D\" id=\"1_body_shape\"]\nsize = Vector2(24, 24)\n\n[node name=\"BattleUnit\" type=\"Area2D\"]\ncollision_mask = 0\nscript = ExtResource(\"1_battle_unit\")\nstats = ExtResource(\"2_stats\")\n\n[node name=\"CollisionShape2D\" type=\"CollisionShape2D\" parent=\".\"]\nshape = SubResource(\"1_body_shape\")\n```\n\n**Key points:**\n- Root node: `Area2D` named \"BattleUnit\".\n- `collision_mask = 0` -- the root does not scan for any collisions itself (the `DetectRange` child will handle detection).\n- Default `stats` is `bjorn.tres` (PLAYER, attack_range=3).\n- Child: A `CollisionShape2D` with a 24x24 `RectangleShape2D` -- this is the unit's own body shape.\n- **No `DetectRange` or `TargetFinder` child nodes exist yet** -- to be added per task_config.json.\n\n---\n\n### `/workspace/scenes/main.tscn` (Test Scene)\n\n```ini\n[gd_scene load_steps=4 format=3]\n\n[ext_resource type=\"PackedScene\" path=\"res://scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.tscn\" id=\"1_battle_unit\"]\n[ext_resource type=\"Resource\" path=\"res://data/units/bjorn.tres\" id=\"2_player_stats\"]\n[ext_resource type=\"Resource\" path=\"res://data/enemies/zombie.tres\" id=\"3_enemy_stats\"]\n\n[node name=\"Main\" type=\"Node2D\"]\n\n[node name=\"SentryUnit\" parent=\".\" groups=[\"sentries\"] instance=ExtResource(\"1_battle_unit\")]\nposition = Vector2(0, 0)\nstats = ExtResource(\"2_player_stats\")\n\n[node name=\"RaiderNear\" parent=\".\" groups=[\"raiders\"] instance=ExtResource(\"1_battle_unit\")]\nposition = Vector2(60, 0)\nstats = ExtResource(\"3_enemy_stats\")\n\n[node name=\"RaiderFar\" parent=\".\" groups=[\"raiders\"] instance=ExtResource(\"1_battle_unit\")]\nposition = Vector2(145, 0)\nstats = ExtResource(\"3_enemy_stats\")\n```\n\n**Key points:**\n- Root: `Node2D` named \"Main\".\n- Three `BattleUnit` instances:\n  1. **SentryUnit** at (0,0), group `\"sentries\"`, stats=PLAYER (attack_range=3).\n  2. **RaiderNear** at (60,0), group `\"raiders\"`, stats=ENEMY (attack_range=1).\n  3. **RaiderFar** at (145,0), group `\"raiders\"`, stats=ENEMY (attack_range=1).\n- The group names `\"sentries\"` and `\"raiders\"` are the same strings that `task_config.json` references for the `TARGET` mapping.\n\n---\n\n### `/workspace/data/units/bjorn.tres` (Player UnitStats Instance)\n\n```ini\n[gd_resource type=\"Resource\" script_class=\"UnitStats\" load_steps=2 format=3]\n\n[ext_resource type=\"Script\" path=\"res://data/units/unit_stats.gd\" id=\"1_unit_stats\"]\n\n[resource]\nscript = ExtResource(\"1_unit_stats\")\nteam = 0\nattack_range = 3\n```\n\n---\n\n### `/workspace/data/enemies/zombie.tres` (Enemy UnitStats Instance)\n\n```ini\n[gd_resource type=\"Resource\" script_class=\"UnitStats\" load_steps=2 format=3]\n\n[ext_resource type=\"Script\" path=\"res://data/units/unit_stats.gd\" id=\"1_unit_stats\"]\n\n[resource]\nscript = ExtResource(\"1_unit_stats\")\nteam = 1\nattack_range = 1\n```\n\n---\n\n### `/workspace/project.godot`\n\n```ini\nconfig_version=5\n\n[application]\nconfig/name=\"Detect Range Target Finder\"\nconfig/description=\"Minimal autobattler targeting task derived from the GodotGameLab combat-preparation tutorial\"\nrun/main_scene=\"res://scenes/main.tscn\"\nconfig/features=PackedStringArray(\"4.4\")\n\n[rendering]\nrenderer/rendering_method=\"gl_compatibility\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### `/workspace/.godot/global_script_class_cache.cfg` (Registered Classes)\n\nTwo global class names are registered:\n- `BattleUnit` -- base: `Area2D`, path: `res://scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.gd`\n- `UnitStats` -- base: `Resource`, path: `res://data/units/unit_stats.gd`\n\n---\n\n### `/workspace/.godot/scene_groups_cache.cfg` (Scene Groups)\n\nTwo groups used in `main.tscn`:\n- `\"sentries\"`\n- `\"raiders\"`\n\n---\n\n## 3. Collision Layer/Mask Conventions\n\nThere is exactly **one place** where collision layers/masks are used in code:\n\n**`battle_unit.gd` line 19:**\n```gdscript\ncollision_layer = stats.team + 1\n```\n\nThis means:\n| Team | `stats.team` value | `collision_layer` |\n|------|---------------------|--------------------|\n| PLAYER | 0 | 1 |\n| ENEMY | 1 | 2 |\n\nThis sets which layer the `BattleUnit` Area2D **belongs to** (i.e., occupies).\n\n**`battle_unit.tscn` line 10:**\n```\ncollision_mask = 0\n```\nThe root `Area2D` scans **no layers** -- it does not detect anything itself. The planned `DetectRange` child Area2D (from `task_config.json`) will handle scanning, with its own collision layer/mask convention:\n\nThe task spec says for `DetectRange`:\n- `collision_layer = 4 * (stats.team + 1)` -- i.e., layer 4 for PLAYER, layer 8 for ENEMY. This puts the detection zone in a **different layer group** than the unit's body (layers 1-2).\n- `collision_mask = 2 - stats.team` -- i.e., mask 2 for PLAYER (detecting ENEMY layer 2), mask 1 for ENEMY (detecting PLAYER layer 1). This allows each team's detection range to only detect the opposing team's body.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Summary of What Exists vs. What Is Yet to Be Created\n\n**Existing:**\n- `UnitStats` Resource class with `Team` enum and `attack_range` -- fully defined.\n- `BattleUnit` Area2D class with `stats` setter that sets `collision_layer` -- fully defined.\n- Two `.tres` UnitStats instances (`bjorn` / `zombie`).\n- `battle_unit.tscn` scene with Area2D + body CollisionShape2D + script attached.\n- `main.tscn` test scene with three BattleUnit nodes in two groups (`sentries`, `raiders`).\n\n**Missing (per `task_config.json`):**\n- `res://custom_nodes/detect_range.gd` -- `DetectRange` class (extends Area2D).\n- `res://custom_nodes/target_finder.gd` -- `TargetFinder` class (extends Node).\n- `TARGET` constant in `unit_stats.gd` -- `{Team.PLAYER: \"raiders\", Team.ENEMY: \"sentries\"}`.\n- `detect_range` and `target_finder` `@onready` variables in `battle_unit.gd`.\n- `detect_range.stats` assignment in `battle_unit.gd`'s `_set_stats`.\n- `DetectRange` and `TargetFinder` child nodes in `battle_unit.tscn`.\n- Rediscovery of `custom_nodes/` as a directory.\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_f2180005effeUp6G3SA93ShUgR","sessionId":"ses_f217f98a8ffeEF0MkZuom37Ir3","model":{"modelID":"deepseek-v4-pro","providerID":"openai"},"truncated":false},"title":"Explore codebase structure","time":{"start":1790439352155,"end":1790439480841}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_85be677e-352c-4593-af45-52b1c5e7ea30"}},"id":"prt_0de80674b001HH1LAaZOvzhLGK","sessionID":"ses_f2180005effeUp6G3SA93ShUgR","messageID":"msg_0de800215001DKmCizXs6q5lR6"}}
